<!--
  Renders a single "Up next" card below a show view, linking to the
  chronologically-newer post in the same collection. "Next" means
  strictly newer — at the newest post the section is suppressed
  rather than falling back to an older neighbour (which would
  contradict the label).

  Reuses the `_post_list` index card so the single "Up next" entry
  reads like a regular index row — cover-left, title / date /
  description on the right at desktop, stacked on mobile. There's
  only ever one up-next post, so the full index treatment fits;
  the related grid below uses a different (compact, multi-card)
  shape for its many-card case.

  Heading style matches `.related__heading` (small uppercase muted)
  so the show-view tail still reads as a coherent run of sections —
  it's the card body that differs.

  Usage:
      <%%= render 'partials/next_item' %>

  Config (per collection in config/site.yml):

      collections:
        posts:
          next:
            enabled: true       # set false to suppress the section

  Renders nothing when the source is the newest in its collection,
  there's no next page, or `next.enabled` is false.
-->
<% next_post = site.next_in_collection(page) %>
<% if next_post %>
<section class="next-item" aria-labelledby="next-item-heading">
  <h2 id="next-item-heading" class="next-item__heading">Up next</h2>
  <%== render 'partials/post_list', posts: [next_post] %>
</section>
<% end %>
